.git

# Every Dockerfile copies the whole context into its build stage, so anything a
# checkout holds locally reaches an image layer unless it is named here. A
# worktree's `.env` names its own databases, an agent directory carries session
# state, and a log directory carries whatever a local run recorded.
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
**/secrets.env
.claude
**/.claude
logs
**/logs
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-home
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.build
**/.venv
coverage
**/coverage
docs/benchmarks/results

# Generated site outputs. Git ignores them because the site build writes each one, and the image
# build runs that build again. A checkout keeps whatever an earlier local build wrote, including
# twins of pages whose sources are gone, and `COPY . .` would publish them (SM-855).
# site/scripts/image-context.test.ts keeps this list in step with .gitignore.
**/.source
site/public/robots.txt
site/public/sitemap.xml
site/public/llms.txt
site/public/llms-full.txt
site/public/docs.md
site/public/docs
site/public/blog
site/public/404.md
site/public/404.json
site/public/openapi.json
site/public/about.md
site/public/contact.md
site/public/privacy.md
